---
profile: basic

# var-naming[no-role-prefix] wants every role variable prefixed with the
# role's own name (e.g. elasticsearch_http_port). This project instead uses
# a shorter, deliberate convention documented throughout CLAUDE.md,
# inventory/group_vars/, and the role templates: es_*/apm_server_*/etc. for
# public vars (chosen so cross-host references like apm_server_port read
# naturally from other roles), and a leading underscore for
# internal/registered facts (_health, _dpkg_arch, ...). Renaming everything
# to satisfy this rule would be a large, purely cosmetic, cross-cutting
# change across docs and templates with no functional benefit.
skip_list:
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
